From a96a9e84e18fb3d81637435365686bd9878b3568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien MOYAUX <49562406+adrienm7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:57:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(console): center native debug windows at a shared
 minimum size

Debug consoles opened at their small native size and separate menu and
gesture callers bypassed placement. Give each desktop driver one owner
that reads the minimum ratios from the shared UI manifest.

Preserve larger dimensions and existing placement. Windows targets only
the script's own window; macOS reads and applies geometry after the native
console exists. Linux has no native console and remains excluded.

Cover owned-window targeting, deferred work, native refusals and layout
preservation, and guard both production trees against bypassing the owners.
